WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.515
So, what is agentic AI?

00:00:03.896 --> 00:00:06.128
In part one, we looked inside the brain:
it plays word chain,

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:10.136
and different models
have different strengths.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.876
But a brain alone,
like a web chatbot, only talks.

00:00:15.051 --> 00:00:19.138
It can't open your files,
run your programs, or check the results.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.767
Agentic AI gives the brain
a suit of tools, so it can act:

00:00:25.032 --> 00:00:28.027
read files, run programs,
and check the results.

00:00:28.967 --> 00:00:30.245
Think of Iron Man.

00:00:30.674 --> 00:00:32.069
Tony Stark is the brain.

00:00:32.351 --> 00:00:34.252
The suit gives him tools and power.

00:00:34.516 --> 00:00:36.267
Together, they make a hero.

00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:41.752
In AI, ChatGPT is the brain,
and Codex is the suit.

00:00:42.297 --> 00:00:46.915
The suit lets the brain open files,
run code, and fix its own mistakes.

00:00:47.867 --> 00:00:50.435
Inside, an agent works in a loop.

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:51.938
You give it a request.

00:00:52.271 --> 00:00:55.033
The model thinks,
and asks: do I need a tool?

00:00:55.482 --> 00:00:59.448
If yes, it runs the tool,
looks at the result, and thinks again.

00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:02.071
If not, it gives you the final answer.

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:06.121
Say you ask for a chart from a CSV file.

00:01:06.374 --> 00:01:09.267
It writes a script and runs it,
sees an error, fixes the script,

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:12.901
and runs it again,
until the chart is done.

00:01:13.867 --> 00:01:18.132
There are three big families,
each pairing a brain with a suit:

00:01:18.591 --> 00:01:21.892
ChatGPT with Codex,
Gemini with Antigravity,

00:01:22.083 --> 00:01:23.835
and Claude with Claude Code.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:25.912
Like superheroes.

00:01:26.142 --> 00:01:28.446
ChatGPT with Codex is Iron Man.

00:01:28.792 --> 00:01:31.237
Gemini with Antigravity
is Captain America.

00:01:31.538 --> 00:01:34.216
And Claude with Claude Code
is Doctor Strange.

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:37.751
Each hero has strengths and blind spots.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:42.681
So here is our rule for this course:
don't trust just one hero.

00:01:43.633 --> 00:01:44.899
In the hands-on units,

00:01:45.011 --> 00:01:48.104
we'll mainly use Antigravity
and Claude Code on your laptop:

00:01:48.506 --> 00:01:51.710
one agent does the work,
and another agent checks it.

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:56.616
Brain plus tools makes an agent,
and two agents are better than one.

00:01:57.214 --> 00:01:59.282
Next, let's bring them onto your laptop.
